{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_vtwo_obstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_vtwo_obstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QCollatz"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_vTwo_increases_on_odd_branch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qcollatz_vTwo_increases_on_odd_branch","kind":"theorem","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_vtwo_obstruction.lean#L26-L49","doc":"**The `[2]_q`-adic valuation increases on an odd step** — so it is not a\ndescent measure. Witness `P = -X-2` (`q`-odd, `v_[2] = 0`); the odd-branch\nrelation `[2]_q · Pnext = [3]_q · P + 1` gives `Pnext = -(X+1)²` with\n`v_[2] = 2`. Scope-(a): kills the natural `μ` candidate, not the conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0}]}